368 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (Thermal events represent only a small fraction of the dataset, making the classification task highly imbalanced. To address this issue, we tested different strategies, including class weighting, random oversampling, SMOTE, and threshold moving.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
369 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 207 0 R
/E (Although some methods improved recall, they generally reduced precision and did not lead to a significant increase in the overall F1-score. As a result, we selected the original training strategy without resampling, since it provided the best balance between precision and recall.)
/Pg 21 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
