391 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 857 0 R
/E (Cross-platform telemetry: We planned to use macOS and Linux. But, the semantics differed, so Apple-specific columns were entirely missing on Linux.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
392 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 858 0 R
/E (Prediction horizon: A 1-minute horizon made the task too naive. The model mainly extrapolated the current temperature instead of anticipating future events.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
393 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 859 0 R
/E (Class imbalance: Thermal events were much less frequent than normal samples. Several balancing techniques improved recall but reduced precision, leading to little or no overall gain.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
394 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 860 0 R
/E (Misleading labels: We first gave the model the current CPU temperature to predict future temperature. Since temperature changes slowly, the model could "cheat" by leaning on the present value instead of learning to anticipate.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
