407 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 210 0 R
/E (The experimental results show that telemetry data can effectively predict short-term CPU thermal events, achieving high precision while maintaining a average recall. However, the model still misses a significant number of positive events, suggesting that detecting the earliest stages of CPU overheating remains a challenging task. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
408 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 210 0 R
/E (Another important finding is that all four machine learning models achieved very similar validation performance. This indicates that the current limitation is not the choice of the algorithm, but rather the quality of the available data, the label definition, and the evaluation strategy. Future improvements are therefore more likely to come from better data collection and feature design than from adopting more complex models.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
